
What is constructor in java?
=> Type of methode or block of code, used to initialize to object of class.


Difference between constructor and methode
 -No return type.
 -class name and constructor name must be same.
 - No need to call constructor of class, it will get called as soon as we create an object.


 Note: Even when we don't provide any constructure in class, JVM will provide default constructure.
 Note: First line in my constructor is called to parent class No-arg Constructor, you don't need
       add this line.

      - memory allocated to object always runtime.
      - JVM provide Default constructor, not provide paramitrise constructor.

Note - Non-access modifiers cannot be applied with constructors in Java. By mistake,
       if you apply any other modifiers with constructor except these three access modifiers,
       you will get a compile-time error.

       you not apply privet access modifier with constructor.




Characteristics-
       - The constructor should not have any return type even void also because if there is a return type,
        JVM would consider as a method, not a constructor.

        - A constructor is automatically called and executed by JVM at the time of object creation.
        - The access modifiers of the default constructor should be the same as the access modifier of the class.






Why need of constructor in java?

Type of constructor
1. Default constructor -
      - A constructor that has no parameter is known as default constructor in Java.
      When a class does not declare a constructor, Java compiler automatically adds a constructor for that class.

2. Parametrize constructor
3. No argument constructor


No-argument Vs Default constructor


Constructor chaining :
   - This :  Current class Method/Constructor.
   - Super : Parent class Methode/Constructor.



There are the following ways to call a constructor in Java.

   1. A a = new A();    // Here, A is name of class.
   2. new A();         // It is calling A() constructor.
   3. super();
   4. this();
   5. class.forName(“com.scientecheasy.A”).newInstance();